    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 24-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Initialize thicknesses from the iteration 05 best candidate: [94.52, 44.39, 105.43, 125.49, 60.29, 139.57, 57.24, 132.67, 118.56, 65.78, 125.97, 50.46, 126.63, 57.34, 121.89, 87.85, 135.60, 58.91, 115.89, 87.90, 116.43, 63.74, 72.20, 76.02] nm. Apply strict thickness bounds of 45-120 nm to all layers (clip initial values outside bounds to nearest bound). Use gradient_thickness optimizer with step size reduced to 50% of default value. Spectral objectives: maximize mean transmittance over 800-1500 nm band, maximize mean reflectance over 200-400 nm band. Assume normal incidence, unpolarized light. Evaluate robustness with ±15 nm absolute normal thickness tolerance. Total layer count fixed at 24. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 200-400 nm, 800-1500 nm. soft objectives: High transmission in 800-1500 nm band; High reflection in 200-400 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: Low transmission in 200-400 nm band; Low reflection in 800-1500 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layers <= 30; Materials limited to HfO2 and SiO2.",
